poems.text:
Eustathius on the Iliad: Pindar uses μάτρωας not for the mother's brothers but for her parents. And Stesichorus uses πάτρωα for an ancestor on the father's side, where he makes Amphilochus say:

my father's forefather, the godlike Melampus;

for Amphilochus was son of Amphiaraus son of Oicles son of Antiphates son of Melampus.
